text:
Create the comprehensive dark mode design token specification for the Cymbal UI component library:
- Semantic Color Mapping Table:
  - Light Mode: --bg-canvas: #f8fafc; --bg-surface: #ffffff; --bg-subtle: #f1f5f9; --text-primary: #0f172a; --text-secondary: #475569; --border-default: #e2e8f0; --accent-brand: #4f46e5;
  - Dark Mode: --bg-canvas: #030712; --bg-surface: #0f172a; --bg-subtle: #1e293b; --text-primary: #f8fafc; --text-secondary: #94a3b8; --border-default: #334155; --accent-brand: #818cf8;
- Component Overrides: Form inputs should use dark surface background with lighter border on hover; modals use darker elevated slate surface with semi-transparent white border; badges adjust background opacity to 20% in dark mode to prevent overly bright contrast jarring.
- Token Integration: Update the global Tailwind configuration so classes like bg-surface, text-primary, and border-default automatically adapt without needing manual dark: prefixes in every component markup file.
